---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../lib/site.js';

const title = 'About Us';
const description =
  'Who runs CleanLivingHQ, how it is funded, and the standard we hold ourselves to when we write about a product.';
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="/about"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About CleanLivingHQ</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A small independent site that checks what is behind a product claim
        before repeating it. The ranges will change over time; that approach
        will not.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <section aria-labelledby="why">
        <h2 id="why">Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>
          Cooling and body-care products are sold on numbers that rarely survive
          a follow-up question. "Cools you by twelve degrees." For how long, at
          what humidity, measured how? "99.9% antibacterial." Against which
          organism, to which test standard, after how many washes? Most of the
          time nobody can tell you, and the number is repeated across a hundred
          affiliate sites regardless.
        </p>
        <p>
          We would rather explain how a thing works, state clearly where it
          stops working, and let you decide. That is a slower way to sell
          something and a better way to be worth reading twice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how">
        <h2 id="how">How we are funded</h2>
        <p>
          Affiliate commission. When you buy through some of our links, the
          retailer pays us a percentage, and you pay exactly the same price you
          would have paid anyway.
        </p>
        <p>
          We think that model is fine as long as two things are true: you always
          know when a link is commercial, and the commission never decides what
          we say. Every page carrying an affiliate link says so above the link,
          not in the footer. The full arrangement is on the
          <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> page, and the
          rules we write by are on the
          <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> page.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not accept payment for a favourable review, and we do not take
          free products in exchange for coverage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="cover">
        <h2 id="cover">What we cover right now</h2>
        <p>
          This list grows. The site is deliberately not built around a single
          product category — what stays constant is the standard each new range
          has to meet before it gets a buy button.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong><a href="/cooling-towels">Cooling towels</a></strong> — the
            physics, the limits, and the range we are an affiliate for.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong><a href="/heat-safety">Working safely in heat</a></strong> —
            the part that is not a shopping decision, and the reason the site is
            worth reading even if you never buy anything.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong><a href="/skin">Organic skin and body care</a></strong> —
            arriving later this year, with the full ingredient list published
            before any buy button.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>More to come.</strong> The site is built so a new range slots
            in without rebuilding anything — see the
            <a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a> for the standard any
            new category has to meet before it gets a buy button.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="who">
        <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          CleanLivingHQ is operated by {LEGAL.legalName}, {
            LEGAL.entityType === 'sole-trader'
              ? 'a sole trader'
              : 'a registered company'
          }.
          {LEGAL.address && <span> Our trading address is {LEGAL.address}.</span>}
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not doctors or occupational-health professionals, and we say so
          on every page where it matters. Where we summarise published guidance —
          on heat illness, for example — we say where it comes from and what its
          scope is.
        </p>
        <p>
          Questions, corrections and complaints all go to the same place:
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. If we get something
          wrong, tell us and we will fix it and say that we did.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="note">
        <span class="note-title">Corrections</span>
        <p class="mb-0">
          If you find an error, particularly on the heat-safety pages, please
          email us. We would much rather be corrected than be confidently wrong
          on a page someone is relying on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
